appy and safe.\n  - obstacles: Audrey's pups are facing obstacles in agility classes, which Andrew finds impressive. Audrey saw a behaviorist last Wed for the dogs' abnormal behavior and got tips to try.\n  - dog training course: Audrey is taking a challenging but rewarding dog training course; it's a big time sink but her dogs are already doing great and improving.\n  - puppies and dogs: Audrey has four doggies that she takes care of to keep them happy and healthy. Andrew mentioned he would not want puppies and dogs to be punished.\n  - positive reinforcement training class: Audrey is going to attend a positive reinforcement training class; she saw the flyer at her local pet store and met a friendly dog there.\n  - the doggos: Audrey takes the doggos for walks in the park to relax and clear her mind, as they offer a nature environment.\n  - vet: Audrey took her four dogs to the vet for a check-up, which was chaotic, leading her to plan future visits one dog at a time.\n  - dog owners group: Audrey joined a dog owners group recently to learn better care for her four dogs and meets with the group weekly for tips and to let the dogs play together.\n  - dog grooming course: Audrey took a dog grooming course and learned many techniques, offering to share tips with Andrew.\n  - furry friend: Audrey took her furry kids to the pet salon last Friday where they were groomed, looked cute with shiny coats, and behaved well. Andrew considers his dogs furry friends and feels lucky to have them.\n  - four dogs: Audrey cherishes her four dogs, who always make her smile and give love. She has a tattoo of them and recently returned to the tattoo parlor for more drawings on it.\n  - My dogs: Audrey's dogs enjoy meeting new people. They recently had grooming and look soft and fluffy.\n  - vet trip: Audrey took her four dogs to the vet for a check-up, which was chaotic. She plans to take them one by one next time.\n  - ocean: Audrey took her dogs to the beach over the weekend where the