 chat with an artist about music and art, feeling a creative high. He and Dave previously planned to meet when Dave is in Boston. Dave has taken up photography.\n  - documentaries about artists and their creative process: Calvin watches documentaries about artists and their creative process for inspiration and to learn about the music industry. Calvin asked Dave if a notebook helps him stay connected to the creative process.\n  - producer: A producer gave advice to Calvin to stay true to himself and sound unique, which Calvin found motivating regarding his music direction.\n  - something new: Dave finds purpose in transforming things, like when he creates something new or collaborates, as suggested by his work on a vintage Mustang engine and agreement to create something special with Calvin.\n  - sino y tu estilo: Dave advised Calvin that staying true to 'sino y tu estilo' (your style) is vital, makes music unique, and helps it stand out.\n  - favorite artists: Calvin and an artist discussed their favorite artists, art, and the power of music during an inspiring conversation at a Boston gala.\n  - rap song: Calvin mentioned that details can make a difference, using a well-crafted rap song as an example of something made great by details.\n  - clips: Calvin loves the Miami vibe for the vid clips and is excited to show them after collaborating with artists to create something unique.\n  - artist: Calvin met a cool artist at a Boston gala; they connected over music and art, discussing favorite artists and music's power to connect people.\n  - musician: Calvin is a musician and received a gift from another artist that reminds him to keep hustling.\n  - creative haven: Calvin refers to his 'creative haven' as the place where he pours his heart into music, following a flood incident.\n  - people: Calvin is currently on tour with Frank Ocean and finds juggling work and personal life overwhelming, though he pushes on. He is inspired by people's struggles to create deeper mu