ally and received tips to help with their problems.\n  - pet salon: Audrey took her four dogs to the pet salon last Friday for grooming; the dogs were excited, looked cute, and behaved well.\n  - dogs: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon; they looked cute, groomed, and had shiny coats. Andrew has two dogs, Toby and Buddy. They are considered family members.\n  - Audrey's pups: Audrey made an appointment with an animal behaviorist for her dogs due to abnormal behavior. She also joined a dog owners group to learn better care methods.\n  - Audrey: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon last Friday, noting they looked cute with shiny coats, behaved well, and were happy and safe.\n  - breed: Andrew asked Audrey about her dogs' breed and what they enjoy doing most, following a discussion about dog training and finding dog-friendly spots.\n  - pet store: Audrey went to a pet store last Monday to buy toys for her dogs.\n  - cuatro perros: Audrey has cuatro perros (four dogs) whom she loves; she got a tattoo of them on her arm and took them all to the vet, which was chaotic.\n  - Audrey's dogs: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon last Friday for grooming; they looked cute with shiny coats and behaved well there.\n  - pup-friendly: Andrew asked Audrey about plans for making her new place more pup-friendly after the dogs enjoyed the bigger backyard.\n  - My dogs: Audrey's dogs enjoy meeting new people. They recently had grooming and look soft and fluffy.\n  - puppies and dogs: Audrey has four doggies that she takes care of to keep them happy and healthy. Andrew mentioned he would not want puppies and dogs to be punished.\n  - pooches: Pooches moved to a new place with a bigger backyard for running and exploring. Audrey calmed her pooch, Precious, by petting, hugging, and speaking calmly; patience and practice help establish bonds with pooches.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2023,"context_chars":7849,"retrieval_duration":0.32645177841186523,"response_duration":3.7104034423